ESP32 Classic Bluetooth HID for aily Blockly

The Blockly definitions, generator and AilyClassicHIDProfiles.h adapter are
original ailyProject code, distributed under the MIT license in LICENSE.

This package embeds the production sources of two independent Arduino libraries:
  ESP32ClassicBluetoothHID 0.4.0
  ESP32BluetoothSwitchProController 0.2.0
Their original source files, library.properties, LICENSE and NOTICE files are
preserved. AilyClassicHIDProfiles.h is an additive adapter inside the first
library; it does not replace the underlying Host or Controller implementation.

The Classic library includes EspBle's namespaced precompiled Bluedroid Host,
commit ef09bedf2bf0cdd9d0da10757f9801b417821375, built for ESP-IDF 5.5.5 and
the original ESP32. Artifact SHA256:
d64d3a40a3f598e206c5aaf798e9d8fda5c867b632224ed72a616b1221089421

See src/ESP32ClassicBluetoothHID/NOTICE,
src/ESP32ClassicBluetoothHID/src/esp32/NOTICE and its LICENSES directory for
Apache-2.0 and other third-party notices. Host build and API-header provenance
is retained in src/ESP32ClassicBluetoothHID/extras/host-build/MANIFEST.json.

Nintendo Switch protocol facts are documented in the independent Switch
library's README. No Nintendo firmware, device ROM dump or pairing keys are
included. Switch/PC radio interoperability has not been hardware-tested.
